# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is **already installed and properly configured** in this project. After fetching the latest documentation from Vercel's official quickstart guide and thoroughly reviewing the codebase, I verified that the implementation follows all current best practices for Next.js App Router.

## Current Implementation Status

### ✅ Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 (latest version)
- **Location**: Listed in `package.json` dependencies
- **Status**: Installed and up-to-date

### ✅ Configuration
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.3.2 with App Router
- **Implementation File**: `src/app/layout.tsx` (root layout)
- **Import Statement**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- **Component Placement**: `<Analytics />` component placed correctly in the `<body>` element

### Code Implementation (src/app/layout.tsx)
```typescript
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: Readonly<{
  children: React.ReactNode;
}>) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body className={poppins.className}>
        <Header />
        <main className="pt-16">{children}</main>
        <Analytics />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

